   "title": "How to use · v1.0.0",
   "widgets_values": [
    "## How to use · v1.0.0\n\n**What it does:** Kandinsky 5 Image Lite (6B) text to image at 1024x1024. It follows long prompts and writes short text. Core ComfyUI nodes only.\n\n1. **Your inputs** (green group): write the **Prompt**. Put words you want written in the picture in \"quotes\". Set **Width** / **Height** (1024x1024 default; 1280x768 was tested too), **Steps** (50) and **Seed**.\n2. **Models**: the three loaders must show the files from the Downloads note. Nothing to change.\n3. **Prompt**: the negative prompt box is optional; it is empty by default.\n4. **Sampling**: euler / simple, CFG 3.5, shift 3. These are the model's defaults from the official template.\n5. Press **Run**. The picture is saved by the **Result** node to `output/Kandinsky5/`.\n\n**What to expect:** one 1024x1024 picture in about 1 min 40 s on the test card (50 steps, model load included); 1280x768 took 1 min 28 s. Peak VRAM 12.3 GB.\n\n**Tips**\n- Write long, concrete prompts: the official examples are a full paragraph. The authors say Russian prompts work too (not tested here).\n- The diffusion model file is 12.0 GB, about the size of a 12 GB card, so on 12 GB ComfyUI has to keep part of it in system RAM (not tested on a 12 GB card).\n- Fewer steps = faster. Below 50 was not tested. CFG is on the sampler in group 4.\n\n**Tested on:** RTX PRO 4000 Blackwell 24 GB · 64 GB RAM · ComfyUI 0.45.3 started with --reserve-vram 12 (ComfyUI keeps its models within about 12 GB). **Not verified on a 12 GB card.**\n"
   ]
  },
